<title>DUBAI: Saudi 95 barley imports cost 1.96 billion riyals.</title>
<headline>Saudi 95 barley imports cost 1.96 billion riyals.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia, world's largest barley importer, bought 1.96 billion riyals ($523 million) worth of the grain in 1995, the official Saudi Press Agency (SPA) reported on Sunday.</p>
<p>It said the oil-rich kingdom imported 3.94 million tonnes of barley in 1995 from the United States, Canada, Switzerland, The Netherlands, Britain, Spain, Bulgaria, France, Turkey and the Ukraine.</p>
<p>Analysts expect Saudi Arabia to buy around five million tonnes of barley, or 50 percent of world feed barley trade, this year.</p>
<p>($1=3.75 riyals)</p>
</text>
